## How to read both sides

- `git status` shows where the rebase stands and which files are unmerged.
- `git diff` shows the conflict markers; `git log --oneline ORIG_HEAD..HEAD` the commits the run branch took, and `git show <commit>` each of them.
- `git show REBASE_HEAD` is this task's commit as its session made it.

## The job

1. Produce a resolution in which both this task's intent and the other tasks' intents survive. Edit the files; don't drop one side to make the conflict go away.
2. Don't run `git rebase --continue`, `git rebase --abort`, `git rebase --skip` or `git commit`. Edit files only; igris finishes the rebase (or folds your fix into the task's commit) after your done.
3. Run the project's checks (`make fmt lint test` or whatever the project uses) before you finish.
4. Don't edit the plan or its Status column; igris updates it.

If anything needs the owner — a decision between two incompatible intents, an unclear spec — ask in this chat and wait.

